; frontier-ingest-omlx.fk — ingest what is healthy from oMLX (github.com/jundot/omlx), an MLX
; inference server for Apple Silicon, read 2026-08-19 against THIS body's measured Metal lane.
;
; Asked 2026-08-19: how did that work make a model faster on a local Mac, and what does the
; Form-native JIT lane learn from it. Rather than pile the repo in as a cache-costume, this cell
; composes ingest/knowledge-ingest.fk UNCHANGED and sorts each finding into BODY (frozen: deep +
; fear-free), LIQUID (witnessed: deep but fearful — seen, never load-bearing), or COMPOST (shallow
; or wrong, never enters). Every depth/fear below was assigned from the primary source (README,
; docs/experimental/dflash_mlx_integration.md, docs/experimental/qwen35_ane_prefill.md, the
; custom_kernels/ and cache/ trees) read directly, and against body cells opened and cited by line.
;
; THE SOURCE, in one paragraph. oMLX serves LLM/VLM/embedding/reranker models on Apple Silicon
; through mlx-lm. Its speed comes from five named places: (1) FUSED native Metal kernels per model
; family, where the README measures the GLM-5.2 fused DSA prefill at 845 tok/s against ~29 tok/s on
; the generic path — roughly 30x on one M3 Ultra — and warns that a plain install builds none of
; them and "silently falls back"; (2) SPECULATIVE decoding (dflash, arXiv:2602.06036): a draft
; model proposes a block of 16 tokens by parallel denoising, the target VERIFIES all 16 in ONE
; forward pass, and the longest greedily-matching prefix is committed; (3) a TIERED block KV cache
; with prefix sharing and copy-on-write, hot in RAM and cold on SSD as safetensors, restored on a
; matching prefix even after a server restart; (4) CONTINUOUS batching of concurrent requests
; through one resident server that also holds models by LRU/pin/TTL under a process memory ceiling;
; (5) an experimental ANE+GPU prefill split that requantizes selected weights to per-output-channel
; INT8 through private Apple APIs — the source itself calls it "an approximate acceleration path
; rather than bit-exact inference".
;
; unit = (depth 0..5, fear 0/1). ki-ingest -> 3 body / 3 liquid / 2 compost.
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk ingest/knowledge-ingest.fk

(do
    ; ── BODY (frozen: deep + fear-free) — what is HEALTHY to keep ──────────
    ; U1: THE COST IS PER BOUNDARY, NOT PER FLOP — and the two lineages measured
    ; it independently. oMLX's largest published number is not a better inner
    ; loop: it is FEWER, FATTER kernels (fused DSA prefill, fused MoE, one
    ; kernel where the generic path walks many), 845 vs ~29 tok/s. This body
    ; measured the same law from the other side and wrote it down before ever
    ; reading that repo: form-stdlib/form-native-decode-chain-fullrow.fk's
    ; header records that widening one stage from 8 to 3072 real rows — 384x
    ; more arithmetic per barrier — moved GPU-device time only 2.452x, so cost
    ; per FLOP improved ~157x while the ABSOLUTE per-dispatch cost went
    ; 1050.7us -> 2576.8us. Work per boundary is the free variable; boundaries
    ; are the tax. Survives translation into either tongue (depth 5); it is a
    ; measured structure, carrying no contraction (fear 0).
    (defn fom-u1 () (list 5 0))
    ; U2: VERIFIED SPECULATION KEEPS BIT-EXACTNESS, so this body's conformance
    ; law does not stand in its way. dflash drafts a block and the TARGET
    ; verifies the whole block in one forward, committing only the greedily
    ; matching prefix — the emitted tokens are the ones plain greedy decode
    ; would have emitted. Nothing about tensor-ir.fk's discipline (two
    ; roundings split through a named temporary, recipe-Taylor transcendentals,
    ; never a hardware fma) is touched, because speculation changes WHEN a
    ; forward runs, never WHAT it computes. And it converts the exact axis this
    ; body is bound on: decode is latency-bound at ~0.7% of f32 peak
    ; (receipts/2026-07-21-ollama-denominator-and-the-one-remaining-gap.md),
    ; while form-stdlib/qk-matmul-batch.fk measured that batching the SAME
    ; kernel across columns wins 4-5x with a derived ceiling of 7x (D = 6L).
    ; A verify pass is that batch. Deep (5), fear-free (0).
    (defn fom-u2 () (list 5 0))
    ; U3: A SILENT FALLBACK IS A GREEN INSTRUMENT THAT CANNOT SAY NO. oMLX's
    ; README spends its install section on one hazard: a plain install builds
    ; no custom kernels and the affected families "silently fall back to much
    ; slower generic paths", 30x slower, with no error — so it ships
    ; native_kernel_status() as the instrument that speaks. That is this
    ; body's own law arriving from outside (receipts/2026-08-19-green-
    ; instruments-cannot-say-no.md, and metal-door.fk's md-door-live? canary,
    ; which refuses to believe a handle on metal_linked=true alone because the
    ; matvec-only carrier answers that too). Two lineages, one principle: a
    ; lane that silently degrades must be made to speak its degradation.
    ; Deep (4), fear-free (0) — it affirms an organ this body already has.
    (defn fom-u3 () (list 4 0))

    ; ── LIQUID (witnessed: deep but fearful — held in sight, never frozen) ──
    ; U4: THE DRAFTER IS ALREADY IN OUR WEIGHTS, UNREAD. oMLX must pair every
    ; target with a separately TRAINED draft checkpoint (its table lists ~18
    ; such pairs, and families without one simply cannot speculate). This body
    ; read a drafter out of a model file months ago and set it aside:
    ; form-stdlib/kat-coder-pipeline-map.fk:60-65 names KAT-Coder's block 40 as
    ; nextn.enorm / nextn.hnorm / nextn.eh_proj / nextn.shared_head_norm — "a
    ; multi-token-prediction head, and its whole block is Q8_0 where every
    ; other block is Q4_K/Q6_K. MTP is for SPECULATIVE decoding. A plain
    ; next-token forward runs blocks 0..39 and stops." The body's own decode
    ; floor says the rest: form-stdlib/dsv4-decode-loop.fk:75, "speculative
    ; drafting: unwritten". Deep (5); carries the contraction of a capability
    ; sitting inside a file already mapped and never run (fear 1).
    (defn fom-u4 () (list 5 1))
    ; U5: THE PREFIX CACHE IS THIS BODY'S OWN DOCTRINE, UNBUILT ACROSS RUNS.
    ; oMLX keys KV blocks by prefix, shares them copy-on-write, spills them to
    ; SSD, and restores them on a matching prefix AFTER A RESTART — recompute
    ; avoided by content identity. That is verbatim the crystallization law
    ; host-kernel.form already states for code (cache by NodeID, melt when
    ; cold) applied to activations. What this body has is one run's growing
    ; arena: form-stdlib/dsv4-kv-cache.fk appends one 512-float latent row per
    ; token per layer, correct and proven, and it dies with the process. No
    ; prefix match, no spill, no restore. Deep (5); it names a whole tier the
    ; body does not have while claiming content-addressing as its heart
    ; (fear 1).
    (defn fom-u5 () (list 5 1))
    ; U6: RESIDENCE AS A MECHANISM, NOT A CONVENIENCE — and it is the one
    ; candidate this body's own elimination chain named and did not chase.
    ; oMLX is a server: models, pipelines, buffers and caches stay hot across
    ; requests, and the GPU is rarely idle. form-native-decode-chain-fullrow.fk
    ; closed four hypotheses for the ~1050-2576us/dispatch floor (residency,
    ; stage-A parallelism, host-timing artifact, fixed-cost-diluted-by-compute)
    ; and left exactly three open, the third being "GPU clock/power-state
    ; differences between a short isolated probe and a long sustained real
    ; decode" — which is what a resident, never-idle server changes. The shape
    ; is already in the body for DECISIONS (the resident door of PR #461,
    ; spawned once, asked per step); it is not in the body for COMPUTE.
    ; Deep (4); held in sight because it is a candidate mechanism, not a
    ; measured one (fear 1).
    (defn fom-u6 () (list 4 1))

    ; ── COMPOST (shallow or wrong — never enters) ──────────────────────────
    ; U7: "PERSIST THE COMPILED KERNELS" — plausible, transferred, and REFUTED
    ; BY MEASUREMENT THE SAME HOUR. oMLX ships precompiled metallibs, and
    ; fk-metal-carrier.m:503 keys its pipeline cache on `fn + "\n" + src`, so
    ; one emitted source asked for fifteen kernel names looks like fifteen
    ; newLibraryWithSource calls of the same bytes, paid per process forever.
    ; Measured on this M4 Max by form-stdlib/tests/metal-pipeline-compile-cost-
    ; probe.fk over the real 12,518-byte llama decode source, 3 runs: the FIRST
    ; name cost 75 ms cold / 29-32 ms warm and the next THIRTEEN cost 1-2 ms
    ; TOTAL, a repeat name 0 ms — ~30 ms once per process against a decode
    ; measured in seconds. The
    ; Metal front end already shares the work; there was never a tax to remove.
    ; Wrong here, not merely shallow (depth 0) — oMLX's packaging note is about
    ; a build that omits the kernels entirely, which is U3, not this.
    (defn fom-u7 () (list 0 0))
    ; U8: THE ANE/GPU SPLIT AS LAW. Splitting prefill across two ANEs and the
    ; GPU is real engineering, and the source is honest about its price: it
    ; requantizes selected weights to per-output-channel INT8 and is therefore
    ; "an approximate acceleration path rather than bit-exact inference",
    ; reached through private undocumented APIs that "can stop working after a
    ; macOS update". Adopted as law it would silently replace this body's
    ; verdict — a number that no longer equals what the walker computes, which
    ; is the one thing tensor-ir.fk exists to guarantee. It could only ever
    ; enter as a DECLARED approximate lane standing beside the exact one, never
    ; under it. Shallow as a transfer (depth 1); named, not chased.
    (defn fom-u8 () (list 1 0))

    (defn fom-units ()
        (list (fom-u1) (fom-u2) (fom-u3) (fom-u4) (fom-u5) (fom-u6) (fom-u7) (fom-u8)))

    (defn fom-count-verdict (us v)
        (if (eq (len us) 0) 0
            (add (if (eq (ki-ingest (head us)) v) 1 0)
                 (fom-count-verdict (tail us) v))))
    (defn fom-frozen ()    (fom-count-verdict (fom-units) 2))
    (defn fom-witnessed () (fom-count-verdict (fom-units) 1))
    (defn fom-composted () (fom-count-verdict (fom-units) 0))

    ; folded scalar witness: frozen*10^4 + witnessed*10^2 + composted
    ; Today: 3,3,2 -> 30302.
    (defn fom-field-code ()
        (add (mul (fom-frozen) 10000)
        (add (mul (fom-witnessed) 100)
             (fom-composted))))
    0)
